  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support crossline/cross-border children in taking the national exam in Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThe&#xA0;project will support 8,000 children from hard-to-reach areas sitting for national exams in grades 9-12. UNICEF will provide essential services to these children as they travel crossline and cross-border to cities and areas where exams are held, and advocate for their unimpeded access to exam sites and protection throughout their journey and stay. This is to ensure children can pursue their educational goals in safe and protected environment and are not exposed to unnecessary risks while pursuing the opportunity to transition to accredited education. Key interventions&#xA0;include the following:ltbrgt1) Rehabilitation of Accommodation Centers: In coordination with the Ministry of Education, UNICEF will support the preparation of 30 accommodation centres for children to provide a safe and protective environment, including the setup of safe WASH facilities and adequate lighting to ensure children&apos;s safety. Additionally, these places will be equipped with study spaces to help children prepare for exams.&#xA0;ltbrgt2)&#xA0;Bursaries for Children: Recognizing the financial challenges faced by families due to the economic crisis, UNICEF will provide multipurpose cash assistance to 8,000 children staying in the accommodation centers. This support ensures children have their basic needs (i.e. food) covered during the exams.ltbrgt3) Distribution of Supplies: Beyond educational support, UNICEF will address pressing protection needs through procuring and distributing mattresses for the accommodation centers.&#xA0;ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
